00:01:32.409 --> 00:01:36.610
it, that actually sums up his personality
pretty perfectly as well. Huh.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:41.870
In terms of power, Akutami introduces Todo
as a realistic measuring stick for Itadori

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:46.780
and co. Someone who is a whole level or two
above them all, but more in reach than the

00:01:46.780 --> 00:02:04.200
walking and talking calamity that is Satoru
Gojo. In fact, Todo is undoubtedly one of

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:09.719
the, if not THE strongest among the current
students. And yes, Fushiguro doing a kamikaze

00:02:09.719 --> 00:02:15.239
attack does not count. Despite being only
a second year student, Todo is already a full-fledged

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:20.040
first grade sorcerer. Just so you have some
comparison, that is the same grade as Nanami

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:26.430
or Yaga, who is a school director. As if this
wasn't enough however, most of the time, Todo

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:32.349
doesn't even use his extraordinary cursed
ability, but simply raw physical ability.

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:37.879
Not only does he have a ridiculous amount
of brute strength, but is also surprisingly

00:02:37.879 --> 00:02:46.340
agile. - When things turn dark however, which
pretty much only means special grade kind

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:51.489
of bad, Todo unpacks his innate jujutsu ability:
The Boogie Woogie, that allows him to switch

00:02:51.489 --> 00:02:56.819
the positions of anything with cursed energy
within his range with a clap of his hands.

00:02:56.819 --> 00:03:01.329
He can change himself out with the location
of another person, or switch two different

00:03:01.329 --> 00:03:05.959
parties other than himself as well. -

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:14.709
Now, is this technique powerful? Obviously.
But I want you to appreciate for a moment,

00:03:14.709 --> 00:03:20.219
what an unusual match-up this power is for
a hulk-like guy like Todo. Because once again,

00:03:20.219 --> 00:03:26.939
here, as you know from my other videos, Akutami
loves playing with expectations. Usually,

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:32.430
the trope of the beefcake character in Anime
is kind of predictable. Either he is a lot

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:43.499
weaker and more stupid than all the weak looking
people around him, or he gets a boring power,

00:03:43.499 --> 00:03:47.739
like making his body harder than it already
is... or a big weapon or something...basically

00:03:47.739 --> 00:03:57.939
that's the guy who always goes down first.
The idea being that we as the audience go:

00:03:57.939 --> 00:04:04.090
Oh he looks strong, how will our skinny hero
beat him. And then we are surprised how powerful

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:10.989
the small guy actually is. The trope was basically
dead after David vs Goliath. But it keeps

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:15.189
coming back for some reason.
Anyways, Todo flips that trop on its head

00:04:15.189 --> 00:04:21.060
in the sense that he looks incredibly strong,
and he is incredibly strong. And not only

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:27.009
that he also has an ability that requires
him to basically play 4D chess with his opponent

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:37.310
all the time, trying to figure out if, what,
when and where he is gonna switch. A buff

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:45.180
dude, who is actually buff and has an elegant
ability that requires brains. Hey Anime industry,

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:48.229
Was it really so hard to come up with a character
like this?

00:04:48.229 --> 00:04:55.479
Because on top of his power, oh boy, Todo
is a pretty sharp cookie. Not sure if he's

00:04:55.479 --> 00:05:02.840
530.000 IQ points sharp, as he likes to claim,
but he's definitely no dummy either. So let's

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:07.510
talk about Todo's big brain, and what exactly
is going on in there, so that we can get two

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:24.710
as different sounding exclamations from him
as this - nature, type - So, let's talk about

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.169
Todo's personality.

